MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_001: Lilian, can you tell me what this means? I was told\nthat it's a symbol unique to Saramis.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_002: Oh, the knot? What do you wanna know about\nthat for?
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_003: Our kingdoms have formed an alliance. I think we\nought to learn about each other's cultures.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_004: I knew you didn't have a written language, but I'm\nintrigued that you use a few symbols anyway.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_005: You've done your homework. But are you sure you\nwant to learn about this from me?
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_006: Why not? You've a native Saraminian, aren't you?
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_007: Yeah, but you're tight with the king of Brezarant.\nYou gotta be careful who you talk to.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_008: Back in Saramis, there was a fight over who'd get\nthe throne, and my dad backed the wrong house.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_009: So things with me are kinda...delicate. I get a lot of\ndirty looks back home.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_010: I get a lot of dirty looks back home. Though Queen\nTheodora doesn't seem to care much.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_011: I see. Thanks for the warning. Maybe we should\navoid associating in public.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_012: But we are comrades in arms. Wouldn't it be strange\nif we never spoke at all?
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_013: My kingdom had succession troubles of its own, so I\ncan see where you're coming from.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_014: The Zodiac Incident, right? I've heard of it, but that's\nabout all.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_015: I'm related by blood to Princess Wittiza, who lost her\nclaim to the throne in the affair.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_016: You're royalty?! For real?
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_017: Though I didn't inherit a bloodmark. But you can see\nhow my house has things in common with yours.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_018: It's interesting that we should meet, don't you think?\nSo I don't mind learning about things from you.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_019: Hm. Hey, Gaitz, did you ever think about becoming\nking yourself?
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_020: Not even once. Nor do I think I'd be suited to it.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_021: But Brezarant went a long time without a king, right?\nNo one ever approached you about the possibility?
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_022: Some did. But I was firm in my refusal, and so\neventually they gave up.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_C_023: You stayed true to yourself. I like that.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_001: I've heard your name on a lot of people's lips lately.\nYou're totally famous.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_002: When you've been a knight as long as I have, you\nstart to get a reputation.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_003: Never would have pegged you as over 70 years old.\nYou look way younger.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_004: It's cool that you've been at it for this long and you're\nstill trying to learn new things.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_005: Ha! Thanks to your lessons, I have some knowledge\nof the symbols of Saramis.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_006: What was I supposed to do after you asked me over\nand over and over again?
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_007: I taught you things from my kingdom as thanks,\ndidn't I? Weapon maintenance, horse feed, and so on.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_008: Sure, I've learned a thing or two. Though I never get\nas fired up about it as you.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_009: You should. The things that locals can teach you are\nsurprisingly valuable.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_010: I once went to the land of Sai as a knight errant and\nlearned no end of things there.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_011: Wow, so you were pretty young when you went over\nthere? What did they teach you?
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_012: Let's see... One thing that left quite an impression\nwas the art of running over water.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_013: Come again?
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_014: I also learned of a method to make even a scorching\nflame feel cool through the power of the mind.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_015: I'm told its practitioners could pluck a stone from\nboiling water, unscathed.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_016: Uhhh... And you saw this happen with your\nown eyes?
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_017: No, I only heard the stories. But it was astonishing\nto learn of the amazing things they could do.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_018: Ah, knew it. They were definitely pulling your leg.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_019: That can't be true. What, then, of the secret method\nfor turning leaves into gold?
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_020: Ahhh... Gaitz, please promise me something.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_021: If you want to learn about Saramis, ask me first.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_022: Or if you want to learn about any other countries, for\nthat matter. Don't go trusting snake-oil salesmen.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_023: Hmm? Alright. It's a promise.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_024: But might I point out—we once discussed the risks of\nassociating.
MID_SE_Gat_Lil_B_025: Yeah...I remember. But somebody's clearly gotta\nstep in here.